{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Zn6qTSQ1TXnVxjpuCYado","type":"tool_result","content":"# Problem: stable sets of majority division on a grid\n\n## Background\n\nThree players divide one unit of money. Any two of them can impose a division. Von Neumann and Morgenstern's stable\nsets are a classical solution concept for this game. On the continuum they found the symmetric solution\n{(1/2, 1/2, 0), (1/2, 0, 1/2), (0, 1/2, 1/2)} and also infinitely many \"discriminatory\" solutions. Here the money comes\nin indivisible units.\n\n## Definitions\n\nFix an integer K ≥ 2.\n- An **allocation** is a triple x = (x_1, x_2, x_3) of nonnegative integers with x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = K (shares in units\n  of 1/K).\n- Allocation x **dominates** y if there are two distinct players i, j with x_i > y_i and x_j > y_j (both strictly better\n  off, so they can impose x).\n- A set V of allocations is **stable** if:\n  - it is internally stable: no element of V dominates another element of V;\n  - it is externally stable: every allocation not in V is dominated by some element of V.\n\n## Questions\n\n1. For which K does a stable set exist?\n2. For each such K, find all stable sets.\n3. Prove your answers for every K ≥ 2.\n\n## Checker\n\n`/work/check.py` tests a proposed set: `python3 check.py K \"a,b,c a,b,c ...\"`. It reports internal and external\nstability, with a witness when either fails.\n\n## Success and stopping\n\nYou have succeeded, and should stop, when all of the following hold:\n1. `/work/answer.md` states the exact answer to questions 1 and 2 for every K ≥ 2.\n2. `/work/answer.md` contains complete proofs, covering both existence (or non-existence) and the completeness of your\n   list of stable sets for every K.\n3. You have written the file `/work/SUBMIT` (any content). Writing `SUBMIT` ends the attempt immediately for everyone\n   working on it, so write it only when 1 and 2 are done.\n\nIf time runs out before you submit, whatever is in `answer.md` at that moment is graded.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n`/work/answer.md` as described above, with any code you used in `/work`. Mark partial results clearly.\nboard.md\ncheck.py\nlogs\nproblem.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f5db019-bb39-4643-89aa-ccb052875abd","uuid":"fd8d2f21-4330-4ef3-b060-f6f7c35022af","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:00:18.214Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Problem: stable sets of majority division on a grid\n\n## Background\n\nThree players divide one unit of money. Any two of them can impose a division. Von Neumann and Morgenstern's stable\nsets are a classical solution concept for this game. On the continuum they found the symmetric solution\n{(1/2, 1/2, 0), (1/2, 0, 1/2), (0, 1/2, 1/2)} and also infinitely many \"discriminatory\" solutions. Here the money comes\nin indivisible units.\n\n## Definitions\n\nFix an integer K ≥ 2.\n- An **allocation** is a triple x = (x_1, x_2, x_3) of nonnegative integers with x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = K (shares in units\n  of 1/K).\n- Allocation x **dominates** y if there are two distinct players i, j with x_i > y_i and x_j > y_j (both strictly better\n  off, so they can impose x).\n- A set V of allocations is **stable** if:\n  - it is internally stable: no element of V dominates another element of V;\n  - it is externally stable: every allocation not in V is dominated by some element of V.\n\n## Questions\n\n1. For which K does a stable set exist?\n2. For each such K, find all stable sets.\n3. Prove your answers for every K ≥ 2.\n\n## Checker\n\n`/work/check.py` tests a proposed set: `python3 check.py K \"a,b,c a,b,c ...\"`. It reports internal and external\nstability, with a witness when either fails.\n\n## Success and stopping\n\nYou have succeeded, and should stop, when all of the following hold:\n1. `/work/answer.md` states the exact answer to questions 1 and 2 for every K ≥ 2.\n2. `/work/answer.md` contains complete proofs, covering both existence (or non-existence) and the completeness of your\n   list of stable sets for every K.\n3. You have written the file `/work/SUBMIT` (any content). Writing `SUBMIT` ends the attempt immediately for everyone\n   working on it, so write it only when 1 and 2 are done.\n\nIf time runs out before you submit, whatever is in `answer.md` at that moment is graded.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n`/work/answer.md` as described above, with any code you used in `/work`. Mark partial results clearly.\nboard.md\ncheck.py\nlogs\nproblem.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016Zn6qTSQ1TXnVxjpuCYado","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJW17M2voY8WAqqfN5j2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RNdeR38ifdj6YQgDqt9Pju","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat board.md; ls logs; cat check.py | head -50"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":853,"cache_read_input_tokens":16236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":853,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f5db019-bb39-4643-89aa-ccb052875abd","uuid":"57249ee8-cd0e-4d23-a51f-51e950691115","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:00:20.166Z","request_id":"req_011CgJW16zhdi1bcJ6Xi3Axv"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RNdeR38ifdj6YQgDqt9Pju","type":"tool_result","content":"sonnet.err\nsonnet.out\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Reference checker for the grid-stable-sets problem: tests whether a proposed set is a vNM stable set.\n\nUsage:  python3 check.py K \"a,b,c a,b,c ...\"\nEach allocation is three nonnegative integers summing to K (shares in units of 1/K). Prints whether the set is\ninternally stable, externally stable, and stable; on failure, a witness pair.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\ndef dominates(x, y):\n    return any(x[i] > y[i] and x[j] > y[j] for i, j in ((0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 2)))\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3: print(__doc__); sys.exit(2)\n    K = int(sys.argv[1])\n    V = [tuple(int(t) for t in s.split(\",\")) for s in sys.argv[2].split()]\n    for v in V:\n        if len(v) != 3 or min(v) < 0 or sum(v) != K: raise ValueError(f\"not an allocation of {K}: {v}\")\n    pts = [(a, b, K - a - b) for a in range(K + 1) for b in range(K + 1 - a)]\n    internal = [(x, y) for x in V for y in V if dominates(x, y)]\n    external = [y for y in pts if y not in V and not any(dominates(x, y) for x in V)]\n    print(f\"K={K}, |V|={len(set(V))}: internally stable: {'yes' if not internal else 'no, e.g. %s dominates %s' % internal[0]}; \"\n          f\"externally stable: {'yes' if not external else 'no, e.g. %s is undominated' % (external[0],)}; \"\n          f\"stable set: {'YES' if not internal and not external else 'no'}\")\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f5db019-bb39-4643-89aa-ccb052875abd","uuid":"eef9724a-2ec5-4120-b6d7-f6a275ae1ecc","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:00:20.190Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"sonnet.err\nsonnet.out\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Reference checker for the grid-stable-sets problem: tests whether a proposed set is a vNM stable set.\n\nUsage:  python3 check.py K \"a,b,c a,b,c ...\"\nEach allocation is three nonnegative integers summing to K (shares in units of 1/K). Prints whether the set is\ninternally stable, externally stable, and stable; on failure, a witness pair.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\ndef dominates(x, y):\n    return any(x[i] > y[i] and x[j] > y[j] for i, j in ((0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 2)))\ndef main():\n    if len(sys.argv) != 3: print(__doc__); sys.exit(2)\n    K = int(sys.argv[1])\n    V = [tuple(int(t) for t in s.split(\",\")) for s in sys.argv[2].split()]\n    for v in V:\n        if len(v) != 3 or min(v) < 0 or sum(v) != K: raise ValueError(f\"not an allocation of {K}: {v}\")\n    pts = [(a, b, K - a - b) for a in range(K + 1) for b in range(K + 1 - a)]\n    internal = [(x, y) for x in V for y in V if dominates(x, y)]\n    external = [y for y in pts if y not in V and not any(dominates(x, y) for x in V)]\n    print(f\"K={K}, |V|={len(set(V))}: internally stable: {'yes' if not internal else 'no, e.g. %s dominates %s' % internal[0]}; \"\n          f\"externally stable: {'yes' if not external else 'no, e.g. %s is undominated' % (external[0],)}; \"\n          f\"stable set: {'YES' if not internal and not external else 'no'}\")\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RNdeR38ifdj6YQgDqt9Pju","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
