{"duration_api_ms":117549,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9f5db019-bb39-4643-89aa-ccb052875abd","total_cost_usd":0.21144799999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21197,"cache_read_input_tokens":81055,"output_tokens":15033,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11056},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21197},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":15033,"cacheReadInputTokens":81055,"cacheCreationInputTokens":21197,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21144799999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":11056,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"A stable set exists exactly when K is even. For K = 2h the only stable set is {(0,h,h), (h,0,h), (h,h,0)}. For odd K there is none. The full proof is in `/work/answer.md`, and I wrote `/work/SUBMIT`.\n\nI confirmed the pattern by exhaustive search for K = 2 to 9 with `bf.py`. It finds one stable set for K = 2, 4, 6, 8 and none for K = 3, 5, 7, 9. I did not run `check.py` separately, and I did not run the search beyond K = 9.\n\nThe proof runs as follows:\n\n1. **Existence for even K.** The symmetric set is internally stable. For external stability, an allocation not dominated by any of the three would need two coordinates ≥ h, and with sum 2h that forces it to be one of the three.\n2. **Pairs in V.** In any stable set, two distinct elements agree in exactly one coordinate and differ in the other two.\n3. **Shared coordinate.** If every pair agrees in the same coordinate, some allocation is dominated by no element, so V is not stable.\n4. **Triangle.** Otherwise V is a triangle {a, b, c}, where a = (p,q,r), b = a + d(e₂−e₃) and c = a + d(e₁−e₃). A fourth element is impossible.\n5. **d > 0.** For each case there is an explicit allocation outside V that nothing in V dominates.\n6. **d < 0.** The same kind of explicit allocation exists unless p = q = h and r = 0. That forces K = 2h and the symmetric set.","ttft_ms":2006,"type":"result","duration_ms":117739,"uuid":"154c7cc6-e066-4623-b3dc-dec7a746cf61","ttft_stream_ms":1817,"time_to_request_ms":86,"first_content_frame_ms":1817,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":15033,"cacheReadInputTokens":81055,"cacheCreationInputTokens":21197,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21144799999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":11056,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
